{:edb/db-before-t 2362 :edb/db-after-t 2363 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535675 50 #inst "2026-10-09T04:53:44.936Z" 13194139535675 true] [17592186124406 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360616 13194139535675 true] [17592186124406 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360630 13194139535675 true] [17592186124511 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360602 13194139535675 true] [17592186124511 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360609 13194139535675 true] [17592186124511 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360623 13194139535675 true] [17592186360602 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360603 13194139535675 true] [17592186360602 1089 "q-107112" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360602 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535675 true] [17592186360602 1100 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $C={[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a\\in R}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $C$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $C$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $C$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360602 1113 #uuid "60eef387-3891-5b06-9190-577fe6b6981a" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360602 1145 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $C,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{a}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -({a}_{1}+{a}_{2})\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $C$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}ka & 0 \\\\ 0 & -ka\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $C.$ So, $C$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $C$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360604 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360605 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360606 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360607 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360608 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1041 "selection" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360606 13194139535675 true] [17592186360603 1110 #uuid "15338ece-a3d5-5ad7-b8e8-4bd9f637bd25" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360604 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360604 1111 #uuid "9d78cdcc-a214-5760-88d0-befcef5f983e" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360605 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360605 1111 #uuid "c66c6547-993f-5602-82a0-b7f332428e60" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360606 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360606 1111 #uuid "9feb8f2f-4d8c-551c-a50b-4bc356f78e95" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360607 1034 "IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360607 1111 #uuid "9644ad1a-de21-547c-b426-16ac4ee3dff9" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360608 1034 "II only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360608 1111 #uuid "e12fbf74-305a-5c82-a847-3968c53f6116" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360609 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360610 13194139535675 true] [17592186360609 1089 "q-107113" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360609 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535675 true] [17592186360609 1100 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $A={[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,a,b\\in R}.$  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $A$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $A$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360609 1113 #uuid "6511708a-ae52-5c53-bdf3-d211b27f9e51" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360609 1145 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ and ${A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]$ are two matrices from $A,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{1} & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & {a}_{1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {b}_{1}+{b}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is an element of $A$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kA & =k[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ b & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & ka \\\\ kb & 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $A.$ So, $A$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $A$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360611 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360612 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360613 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360614 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360615 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1041 "selection" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360613 13194139535675 true] [17592186360610 1110 #uuid "93360677-739a-5139-87b0-a1cc9358dd16" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360611 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360611 1111 #uuid "0e4ed195-fdfd-5512-a815-9f6efa29a4dc" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360612 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360612 1111 #uuid "086e4b43-fecd-5ade-96e5-324132e8528e" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360613 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360613 1111 #uuid "f2512662-56ce-5a3a-a8c7-993127cb6087" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360614 1034 "IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360614 1111 #uuid "3f7046a8-8aa6-50b5-8b81-69154f408f01" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360615 1034 "II only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360615 1111 #uuid "5bd29fc3-0eac-5599-844d-2ec3a8dffc67" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360616 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360617 13194139535675 true] [17592186360616 1089 "q-107143" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360616 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535675 true] [17592186360616 1100 "Consider the vector space $C[0,1]$ of all continuous functions $f:[0,1]\\to R$ and its subset $M$ containing all functions that return an integer value at $x=1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $M$ is closed under function addition\n- $M$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $M$ is a subspace of $C[0,1]$\n- $M$ is **not** a subspace of $C[0,1]$" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360616 1113 #uuid "b507c1f4-d8e7-5cb2-9ef0-485dee50d613" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360616 1145 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, if $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are functions from $M,$ then $f(1)$  and  $g(1)$ are integers and so $(f+g)(1)=f(1)+g(1)$ must be an integer number too. So, $M$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, $f(x)=1$ is a function in $M$, but $0.5f(x)$ is not in $M$ because\n$(0.5f)(1)=0.5\\cdot f(1)=0.5$ is not an integer. So, $M$ is *not*  closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is false, while statement IV is true. $M$ is *not* a subspace because it's not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360618 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360619 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360620 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360621 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360622 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1041 "selection" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360618 13194139535675 true] [17592186360617 1110 #uuid "26b23c42-1774-5dee-8c35-7f1af2c9c89d" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360618 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360618 1111 #uuid "953be217-94d5-5eba-b620-b976e7c12eb0" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360619 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360619 1111 #uuid "e38f61a9-9a2b-58b0-a88f-5fa46f67b022" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360620 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360620 1111 #uuid "d4d701f0-394c-5884-9f25-a3b3d23e226c" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360621 1034 "IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360621 1111 #uuid "6f0f2c2e-b16f-581c-8673-d8bf47534538" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360622 1034 "II only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360622 1111 #uuid "399bb6cc-edd7-51ab-b165-8af9903ad686" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360623 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360624 13194139535675 true] [17592186360623 1089 "q-43775" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360623 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535675 true] [17592186360623 1100 "Consider the vector space ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\\times 2$ matrices over $R$ and its subset $E$ containing all $2\\times 2$ matrices of the form $\\alpha A$ where $A$ is some fixed $2\\times 2$ matrix and $\\alpha \\in R.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $E$ is closed under matrix addition\n- $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $E$ is a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$\n- $E$ is **not** a subspace of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360623 1113 #uuid "60087cbe-41e4-5844-91aa-1e5069d8dad8" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360623 1145 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. If ${A}_{1}={\\alpha }_{1}A$ and ${A}_{2}={\\alpha }_{2}A$ are two matrices from $E,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} & ={\\alpha }_{1}A+{\\alpha }_{2}A=({\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{2})A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $B=\\alpha A$ is an element of $E$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}kB & =k\\alpha A=(k\\alpha )A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a matrix from $E.$ So, $E$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $E$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360625 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360626 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360627 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360628 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360629 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1041 "selection" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360628 13194139535675 true] [17592186360624 1110 #uuid "acb674f6-5ce2-5c57-80fb-790190517c2a" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360625 1034 "I and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360625 1111 #uuid "1a32d547-e346-5f3f-9a38-aa15ddbc48ec" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360626 1034 "II and IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360626 1111 #uuid "7f9c2965-7363-58d3-89d4-4097be2345bb" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360627 1034 "I only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360627 1111 #uuid "355ac00f-d608-5fd2-a380-3f900ec90bc5" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360628 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360628 1111 #uuid "346c2b38-29ab-5943-9356-a400c89b5989" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360629 1034 "IV only" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535675 true] [17592186360629 1111 #uuid "1ba3eac0-5f8a-5c01-9f72-7ef3bb99605b" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360630 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360631 13194139535675 true] [17592186360630 1089 "q-94380" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360630 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535675 true] [17592186360630 1100 "Consider the vector space $C[-5,0]$ of all continuous functions $f:[-5,0]\\to R$ and its subset $B={f\\in C[-5,0]\\,|\\,f(0)=0}.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $B$ is closed under function addition\n- $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $B$ is a subspace of $C[-5,0]$\n- $B$ is **not** a subspace of $C[-5,0]$" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360630 1113 #uuid "e1f3a490-989c-5c43-8660-5db51b62310c" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360630 1145 "Recall that a subset of a vector space is a subspace if it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is  true. If $f(x),g(x)\\in B,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f+g)(0) & =f(0)+g(0) \\\\  & =0+0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under addition.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $f(x)\\in B$ and $k\\in R,$ then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(kf)(0) & =kf(0) \\\\  & =k\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $B$ is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\n- Statement III is true, while statement IV is false. $B$ is a subspace because it's closed under addition and scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139535675 true] [17592186360631 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360632 13194139535675 true] [17592186360631 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360633 13194139535675 true] [17592186360631